{
  "summary": "This study investigated mechanotransduction in pericytes during diabetic retinopathy using an iPSC-derived microphysiological system. The model replicated retinal matrix stiffening observed in diabetes, revealing that progressive matrix stiffening alone induces vascular destabilization by suppressing pericyte signaling molecules via FAK-dependent mechanisms. Inhibition of FAK restored vascular integrity without hyperglycemia, suggesting FAK-dependent mechanotransduction as a druggable target for preventing diabetic retage pathogenesis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Progressive matrix stiffening alone induces vascular defects and pericyte signaling suppression",
    "FAK-dependent mechanotransduction mediates pericyte signaling loss in stiffened conditions",
    "FAK inhibition restores vascular integrity without hyperglyemic exposure"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies matrix stiffening as a key regulator of pericyte-mediated vascular stabilization in diabetic retinopathy, establishing FAK-dependent mechanotransduction as a druggable target for therapeutic intervention."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated enhancing TCR-T cell responses in suppressive tumor microenvironments by targeting TGFβ. Researchers engineered TGFβ-specific chimeric antigen receptors (CARs) coexpressed with an HPV16 E7-targeted TCR. The TGFβ-CARs improved proliferation, cytokine production, and cytotoxicity against HPV16+ tumor cells while reducing Treg differentiation and exhaustion markers. Transcriptional changes included decreased FOXP3 and increased IFNG. In vivo, TGFβ-CAR-expressing T cells reduced tumor burden and prolonged survival in mouse models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TGFβ-CAR coexpressing T cells showed enhanced proliferation and cytokine production against HPV16+ tumor cells",
    "TGFβ-CAR-expressing T cells exhibited reduced exhaustion markers and Treg differentiation after repeated antigen exposure",
    "In vivo, TGFβ-CAR-expressing T cells reduced tumor burden and prolonged progression-free survival in B16-F10 tumor models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes TGFβ-targeting CARs as a strategy to counteract immunosuppressive TGFβ signaling in the tumor microenvironment, potentially improving TCR-T cell persistence and efficacy in suppressive settings."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Post-recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states can durably reprogram immune responses when coinciding with tissue inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and Nlrp3/Il1b expression mediate HFD-induced inflammatory amplification",
    "Chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist post-recovery, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a critical temporal window for dietary interventions to modulate inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates quasi-continuous monitoring of urinary oxalate dynamics using a home-based multimodal sensing platform integrated into standard urine collection buckets. The platform combines electrochemical oxalate sensing with pH and volume measurements to correct matrix drift during sequential urination. It enables 24-hour monitoring under dietary hyperoxaluria, revealing distinct metabolic responses to oxalate loads and providing real-time insights into kidney stone risk. The approach offers immediate feedback for hyperoxaluria management.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Quasi-continuous 24-hour urinary oxalate monitoring via integrated electrochemical sensing",
    "Correction of matrix drift using simultaneous pH and volume measurements",
    "Distinct metabolic response profiles under different dietary oxalate loads"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a practical method for real-time oxalate metabolism assessment in hyperoxaluria, advancing decentralized metabolic monitoring strategies for kidney stone risk management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study compared HIV-seronegative women with and without HIV-1 sexual exposure in a Kenyan cohort to characterize immune responses. It found significantly lower systemic inflammation markers in HIV-exposed individuals, reduced activated CD8+ T cells, increased proliferating CD4+ T cells, and elevated immunosuppressive markers in genital tissues and regulatory T cells. These results suggest potential immune adaptations to HIV-1 exposure that may mitigate infection risk.",
  "key_findings": [
    "HIV-1 exposure linked to lower systemic pro-inflammatory cytokines",
    "Reduced activated circulating CD8+ T cells in exposed individuals",
    "Elevated immunosuppressive markers in genital tissues and regulatory T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings reveal immune adaptations to HIV-1 exposure that may contribute to natural resistance mechanisms, offering insights into immune correlates of protection against HIV-1 infection."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how molecular descriptors and machine learning can predict cycle life in aqueous zinc-ion batteries using interpretable methods. By clustering additives into three categories based on SHAP profiles, the research identifies design rules tied to adsorption energetics, charge-transfer gaps, and hydrogen-bond networks. Predictions for novel additives align closely with experimental results, demonstrating that additive performance depends on specific structural features rather than a single universal descriptor. The approach provides a framework for rational design of stable zinc anodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Additives cluster into three categories governed by adsorption energetics, charge-transfer gaps, and hydrogen-bond network regulation",
    "Predicted cycle life for 2-fluoropyridine-5-carbaldehyde (2FPD) matches experimental data within 6.5% (3218 h vs. 3010 h)",
    "Structural features like aldehydes and fluorine atoms significantly enhance cycle life, with aldehydes alone improving performance from 89 h to 900 h"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes category-specific design rules for zinc anode additives, moving beyond empirical screening to enable interpretable, structure-guided optimization of aqueous zinc-ion battery stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether pluripotent stem cell-derived extracellular vesicles (EVs) can modulate systemic immunity in diabetes therapy. Using PSC EVs from embryonic and induced pluripotent stem cells, the research demonstrated superior suppression of proinflammatory cytokines, reduced T cell activation, and induction of regulatory T cells compared to mesenchym. EVs exhibited unique molecular profiles with pluripotency markers like ROR1 and CD133. Local injections of induced PSC EVs via biomaterial scaffolds improved diabetes-free survival in a type 1 diabetes model by enhancing regulatory T cells and preserving β-cell mass.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PSC EVs outperform mesenchymal stem cell-derived EVs in suppressing proinflammatory cytokines and reducing T cell activation",
    "PSC EVs contain unique pluripotency markers including ROR1, CD133, and miR-302 family members",
    "Local injections of induced PSC EVs increased diabetes-free survival by boosting regulatory T cells and preserving β-cell mass in a type 1 diabetes model"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes pluripotent stem cell-derived extracellular vesicles as a scalable platform for systemic immune modulation in autoimmune diseases, offering a novel approach to induce immune tolerance without requiring cell transplantation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cross-system recycling of spent sodium-ion battery cathodes to enhance Na4Fe3(PO4)2P2.9O7 cathodes. By leaching nickel and manganese from degraded layered oxides (NaNi1/3Fe1/3Mn1/3O2) and co-doping them into the polyanionic cathode, the researchers achieved site-selective optimization. The modified cathode (Na4Fe2.9Ni0.05Mn0.05(PO4)2P2O7) showed improved conductivity, Na+ diffusion, and stability, with 91.2% purity, 92.84% initial coulombic efficiency, 75.21 mAh g-1 at 50 C, and 86.74% capacity retention after 12,000 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Site-selective Ni/Mn co-doping from recycled layered oxides enhances Na4Fe3(PO4)2P2O7 cathode performance",
    "The optimized cathode achieves 91.2% purity, 92.84% initial coulombic efficiency, and 86.74% capacity retention after 12,000 cycles",
    "NFNMPP//HC pouch cells demonstrate 5557 cycles with 82.37% capacity retention at 30 C and a wide operating temperature range (-40°C to 55°C)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a cross-system recycling strategy to transform spent sodium-ion battery cathodes into high-performance polyanionic materials, advancing sustainable cathode optimization for energy storage applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the role of BET inhibitors in modulating the Th17/Treg immune balance in osteosarcoma. Using public datasets, immunohistochemistry, flow cytometry, and xenogeneic mouse models, researchers found a Treg-enriched, Th1.7-deficient state in osteosarcoma patients, particularly in metastatic disease. BETi treatment reduced osteolytic changes and shifted Th17/Treg frequencies in mice, with BRD4 inhibition targeting the CXCL12/CXCR4 pathway. Full-dose BETi improved survival and tumor burden compared to reduced-dose regimens or combinations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Osteosarcoma patients exhibit a Treg-enriched, Th17-deficient immune state, especially in metastatic disease",
    "BET inhibitor treatment attenuated osteolytic changes and modulated Th17/Treg frequencies in mouse models",
    "Full-dose BETi demonstrated superior survival and tumor burden reduction compared to reduced-dose BETi or anti-B7-H3 combinations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies BET inhibition as a viable strategy to reverse immunosuppression in osteosarcoma by restoring Th17/Treg balance, offering a potential therapeutic target for improving anti-tumor immunity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing Cu2O photocathode efficiency for photoelectrochemical water splitting using p+/p homojunction back contacts. The approach involves engineering a homojunction to improve hole-selective extraction and suppress electron backflow at the interface. Results show a hydrogen evolution reaction onset potential of 1.1 V and saturated photocurrent density of ∼8.0 mA cm-2. The design also enables semi-transparent Cu2O photocathodes for tandem solar cell integration, achieving a solar-to-hydrogen efficiency of 7.31%.",
  "key_findings": [
    "p+/p homojunction back contacts improve hole-selective extraction in Cu2O photocathodes",
    "Optimized device achieves a hydrogen evolution reaction onset potential of 1.1 V",
    "Semi-transparent Cu2O photocathodes enable tandem solar cell integration with 7.31% solar-to-hydrogen efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that homojunction engineering in Cu2O photocathodes can significantly enhance charge separation and extraction for efficient photoelectrochemical water splitting."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated genetic links between ferroptosis-related genes and migraine susceptibility using integrated genomic and immunological approaches. By analyzing five migraine GWAS datasets, the researchers identified 13 genes with strong cross-omics evidence (ACADSB, ADAMTS13, CDH1, CHMP1A, DPP4, GCH1, GSTM1, ISCU, MAPK9, MAPK14, MUC1, TFRC, TLR4) and 25 genes with recurrent but incomplete evidence. The findings reveal a peripheral immune-protein network involving B-cell traits, myeloid cells, and inflammatory markers, suggesting potential biomarkers and therapeutic targets for migraine.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Thirteen genes met high cross-omics evidence criteria for migraine susceptibility",
    "Immune-cell MR identified recurrent CD27-related B-cell and CD33-related myeloid traits",
    "PBMC single-cell RNA sequencing showed increased IFNG expression in CD8+ T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genetically validated evidence of a peripheral ferroptosis-immune network implicated in migraine pathogenesis, advancing understanding of migraine's immunometabolic mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ytterbium (Yb)-doped tellurium-selenium (TeSe) alloys to suppress oxidation-induced degradation in p-type semiconductors. The researchers developed a strategy using Yb's strong bonding with tellurium and high oxygen affinity to stabilize TeSe alloys against TeO2 formation. The resulting Te0.7Se0:Yb films achieved a hole mobility of 177.5 cm² V⁻¹ s⁻¹ and enabled ZnO/Te0.7Se0.3:Yb photodetectors with 0.21 A/W responsivity at 1300 nm for short-wave infrared imaging.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Yb doping suppresses Te oxidation to TeO2 in TeSe alloys through strong Te-Yb bonding and high oxygen affinity",
    "Te0.7Se0.3:Yb films achieved 177.5 cm² V⁻¹ s⁻¹ hole mobility",
    "ZnO/Te0.7Se0.3:Yb photodetectors showed 0.21 A/W responsivity at 1300 nm for short-wave infrared imaging"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes Yb-enabled oxidation suppression as a critical mechanism for stabilizing high-mobility p-type TeSe alloys, advancing practical short-wave infrared photodetectors and complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how ultrasound-targeted nanobubble destruction (UTND) combined with anti-CTLA-4 therapy modulates the tumor microenvironment in microsatellite stable colorectal cancer. Using a CT26 mouse model, scRNA-seq and molecular analyses revealed UTND-induced ROS production activating NF-κB signaling to upregulate CCL8 in macrophages. This CCL8-expressing macrophage subpopulation suppressed regulatory T cell function via CCL8-CCR2 signaling, enhancing CD8+ T cell activity and improving tumor response compared to single treatments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "UTND with anti-CTLA-4 suppressed tumor growth in MSS CRC mouse models",
    "UTND promoted ROS-mediated NF-κB activation increasing CCL8 transcription in macrophages",
    "CCL8 from Macro Ccl8 suppressed Treg function through CCL8-CR2 signaling, enhancing CD8+ T cell activity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a ROS-NF-κB-CCL8 axis that UTND activates to overcome immunosuppression in MSS colorectal cancer, providing a mechanistic basis for combining physical interventions with immunotherapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates fluorine-free polymer donors for organic solar cells (OSCs) by designing a dichlorobenzodithiophene-4-8-dione (BDD2Cl) unit. The polymer donor PBDTT-BDD2Cl exhibits deeper energy levels, enhanced crystallinity, and improved solubility compared to fluorinated controls. It achieves higher photovoltage (0.947 V) and lower energy loss (0.182 eV) in thin-film devices (21.1% PCE) and thick-film devices (17.3% PCE), demonstrating cost-effective efficiency gains without fluorine.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PBDTT-BDD2Cl polymer donor shows deeper energy levels and improved crystallinity versus fluorinated BDTT-alt-BDD polymers",
    "Thin-film OSCs achieve 21.1% certified PCE with BDD2Cl, surpassing fluorinated controls (19.3%)",
    "Thick-film devices (500 nm) reach 17.3% PCE, outperforming other thick-film OSCs (≥500 nm)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that fluorine-free benzodithiophene-4-8-dione units can enhance cost-effective organic solar cell performance across thin and thick films without compromising efficiency."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines how myelod. neoplasms (MDS) transform into acute myeloid leukemia (AML) through dynamic interactions between mutant hematopoietic clones and the bone marrow immune microenvironment. It highlights chronic inflammation, immune suppression, and niche remodeling that facilitate clonal expansion and therapy resistance. The study emphasizes integrating genetic and immune features to improve risk stratification and develop microenvironment-targeted therapies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MDS-to-AML transformation involves reciprocal interactions between mutant hematopoietic clones and the bone marrow immune microenvironment",
    "Chronic inflammation coexists with immune suppression including T-cell exhaustion and myeloid-derived suppressor cell expansion",
    "Mutant clones remodel the niche via epigenetic changes and inflammatory-metabolic reprogramming, creating feedback loops that drive therapy resistance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that MDS-to-AML progression is an ecological process driven by immune-niche crosstalk, providing a framework for targeting microenvironmental factors to delay leukemic transformation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the design of polymeric fullerene nanosheet membranes for selective hydrogen transport. By engineering a qTP lattice with in-plane pores converging from 5.87 Å to 3.11 Å, the researchers achieved Ångström-scale molecular discrimination. The membrane demonstrated high H2 permeance (3896 ± 107 GPU) and an H2/CO2 separation factor of 88.5 ± 5.9 for equimolar mixtures at 303.15 K and 100 kPa. Performance remained stable over 200 hours.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered polymeric fullerene nanosheets with in-plane pores converging from 5.87 Å to 3.11 Å",
    "H2 permeance of 3896 ± 107 GPU and H2/CO2 separation factor of 88.5 ± 5.9",
    "Stable separation performance over 200 hours of operation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes topology-encoded pore geometry as a design principle for achieving Ångström-scale molecular discrimination in lamellar membranes, enabling precise control over selective transport pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed and validated a deep learning-based pathomics model using H&E-stained whole slide images to predict natural regulatory T cell (nTreg) infiltration in breast cancer. The model, trained on TCGA data with feature selection via mRMR and RFE, generated a Pathomics Score (PS) that correlated with FOXP3+ cell density and was independently associated with poor overall survival (HR = 1.68, p = 0.008). The PS also identified immune activation pathways and immunosuppressive features in the tumor microenvironment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High nTreg infiltration predicted poor overall survival with a hazard ratio of 1.68 (95% CI 1.15-2.46, p = 0.008)",
    "The Pathomics Score (PS) achieved an AUC-ROC of 0.72 in validation cohort and strongly correlated with FOXP3+ cell density (p < 0.001)",
    "High PS patients exhibited immune activation pathways and immunosuppressive microenvironment features including upregulated immune checkpoint genes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a non-invasive digital biomarker derived from standard histopathology images that quantifies immunosuppressive regulatory T cell infiltration and its prognostic impact in breast cancer, advancing the field of computational pathomics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates lignin-based supramolecular dynamic networks for sustainable flexible electronics. The researchers designed a rigid-flexible supramolecular strategy using lignin-derived domains and dynamic polymer segments to overcome mechanical robustness versus multifunctionality tradeoffs. The resulting ionogel demonstrates high elongation (1564%), strong underwater adhesion (488.3 kPa), self-healing, strain sensing (gauge factor 2.83), and energy harvesting via triboelectric nanogenerators (75 V output). These properties enable integrated mechanical robustness, sensing, and energy harvesting in sustainable electronics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Lignin-derived ionogels achieve 1564% elongation at break",
    "The material exhibits 488.3 kPa underwater adhesion strength on steel",
    "Ionogels function as strain sensors with a gauge factor of 2.83 and stable output over 350 stretching cycles"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes lignin as a versatile platform for dynamic supramolecular networks that integrate mechanical robustness, sensing capabilities, and energy harvesting in sustainable flexible electronics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated immune profiles predicting successful oral immunotherapy (OIT) outcomes in young peanut-allergic children. Using blood samples from 49 participants in a randomised trial, researchers assessed immune cell subsets and FcεR1 expression. OIT achieved desensitisation in 91.3% versus 20.8% of the avoidance group. Key immune markers included expanded basophils, monocytes, and dendritic cells in OIT responders, with younger children and low peanut-specific IgE levels correlating with complete desensitisation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "OIT induced desensitisation in 91.3% of participants versus 20.8% in strict avoidance",
    "OIT responders showed expanded basophils, monocytes, and dendritic cells at 12 weeks",
    "Younger children with low peanut-specific IgE and low CD4+ memory Tregs were more likely to achieve complete desensitisation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies specific immune signatures associated with successful oral immunotherapy outcomes, providing potential biomarkers for monitoring treatment response and predicting desensitisation success in peanut-allergic children."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates molecular engineering strategies to enhance charge transport and reduce nonradiative energy loss in organic solar cells. By integrating sulfur locking and chlorination, the researchers optimized intermolecular packing and excited-state properties. Binary cells achieved 20.0% efficiency with low nonradiative loss (∼0.19 eV) and high open-circuit voltage (0.951 V). Ternary devices incorporating Qx2Ph-SCl further improved efficiency to 21.3% by reducing recombination. The approach demonstrates synergistic effects for high-performance organic solar cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Sulfur locking enhances molecular conformation and intermolecular packing, improving exciton diffusion and charge transport",
    "Chlorination strengthens intermolecular interactions via Cl···S contacts, enabling tighter π-π stacking and crystalline ordering",
    "Binary OSCs with Qx2Ph-SCl achieved 20.0% efficiency and low nonradiative energy loss of ∼0.19 eV"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a synergistic molecular design strategy for simultaneously optimizing charge transport and voltage loss in organic solar cells, advancing the field toward higher efficiency with reduced nonradiative recombination."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated heparanase (Hpse) expression in regulatory T cells (Tregs) and its association with immunotherapy resistance in lung adenocarcinoma. Using immunohistochemistry and single-cell RNA sequencing, researchers found Hpse1 expression in Tregs and macrophages, linked high Hpse1 to poor prognosis, and demonstrated that Hpse-expressing Tregs increase tumor-infiltrating Tregs. PG545, an Hpse inhibitor, reduced Treg invasion into the extracellular matrix and enhanced PD-L1 blockade efficacy in mouse models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Hpse1 expression in Tregs and macrophages was identified via single-cell RNA sequencing",
    "High Hpse1 expression correlates with poor postoperative prognosis in lung adenocarcinoma",
    "PG545 inhibits Treg invasion into HSPG-rich extracellular matrix and synergizes with PD-L1 blockade"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "Hpse-mediated Treg modulation represents a novel mechanism of immunotherapy resistance in lung cancer, highlighting a targetable pathway for improving immunotherapy efficacy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how poly(arylene sulfide sulfone) (PASS)-predefined oxygen/sulfur donor fields direct competitive-cooperative phase evolution in Fe/Co bimetallic systems for cross-band microwave absorption. Using molecularly preorganized donor sites, the researchers enhanced non-equivalent Fe/Co coordination during pyrolysis, generating multiphase heterostructures with optimized dielectric, magnetic, and impedance properties. The CFC-4 absorber achieved -73.83 dB at 6.23 GHz and -76.59 dB at 16.98 GHz, demonstrating effective cross-band absorption from 2 to 18 GHz with a maximum EAB of 5.03 GHz.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PASS-defined O/S donor fields amplify non-equivalent Fe/Co coordination during pyrolysis",
    "CFC-4 exhibits cross-band absorption across 5G and radar frequencies with -73.83 dB at 6.23 GHz",
    "Cumulative effective absorption exceeds 90% over 2-18 GHz with minimal thickness (1-5 mm)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes O/S donor-field engineering as a strategy to enhance cross-band microwave absorption in Fe/Co systems through controlled phase evolution and coordination differentiation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated sex-specific immune responses in mice subjected to chronic unpredictable mild stress (CUMS), a model for depression. Using flow cytometry, it assessed T regulatory (Treg) cells and T-cell activation markers. CUMS induced Treg depletion and elevated CD154/CD152 ratios. Four treatments improved depressive behaviors, with SAMe normalizing the CD154/CD152 ratio. Females showed reduced Treg activity and higher activation ratios than males, indicating significant sex differences in immune regulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CUMS mice exhibited Treg depletion and increased CD154/CD152 ratio",
    "All treatments alleviated depressive behaviors with SAMe normalizing CD154/CD152 ratio",
    "Females had lower Treg activity and higher T-cell activation ratios than males"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate sex-dependent immune dysregulation in depression models, emphasizing the necessity of sex as a biological variable in immune-mediated depression research."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing bamboo's mechanical properties through nanocellulose reinforcement to address its inefficient load transfer in heterogeneous cell walls. By infiltrating cellulose nanocrystals into bamboo cell walls, the researchers reorganized interfacial hydrogen-bonding networks, improving stress transfer and mechanical homogeneity. The material achieved a tensile strength of 0.98 GPa and Young's modulus of 52.7 GPa, with carbon intensity up to two orders of magnitude lower than carbon fiber, demonstrating scalable production of high-performance, low-carbon structural materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cellulose nanocrystals infiltrate bamboo cell walls to reorganize interfacial hydrogen-bonding networks",
    "Enhanced tensile strength (0.98 GPa) and Young's modulus (52.7 GPa) compared to natural bamboo",
    "Carbon intensity reduced by up to two orders of magnitude relative to carbon fiber"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable method to produce high-performance structural materials from abundant biomass, decoupling mechanical strength from carbon footprint through nanoscale reinforcement."
}
